---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Interests — Aly Metwaly"
  description="Fitness and weightlifting, markets and analysis, and how I structure learning outside the day job."
>
  <div class="page-layout">
    <div class="page-content">
      <div class="page-hero">
        <div class="kicker reveal-on-scroll">
          <span class="kicker-dot"></span>
          Beyond the desk
        </div>

        <h1 class="reveal-on-scroll">Interests &amp; hobbies</h1>

        <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
          I keep a few pursuits outside work that sharpen discipline, balance risk with
          curiosity, and turn scattered reading into something I can actually use in
          writing and speaking.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="reveal-on-scroll">Fitness &amp; weightlifting</h2>

      <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
        Training is a steady mix of HIIT sessions and weightlifting blocks I plan
        around travel and long work weeks. I track protein and recovery the same way
        I think about delivery cadence: small, repeatable commitments beat heroic
        bursts that do not last.
      </p>

      <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
        For me, strength work is less about numbers on the bar and more about
        consistency under fatigue—showing up, adjusting when something is off, and
        building resilience I can lean on when professional seasons get intense.
      </p>

      <h2 class="reveal-on-scroll">Investments &amp; market analysis</h2>

      <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
        I run a diversified portfolio and spend time on technical analysis as an
        intellectual outlet—not as a prediction hobby, but as a structured way to
        test hypotheses, manage risk, and stay honest about what I do and do not know.
      </p>

      <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
        Equities anchor most of my allocation, and I also follow commodities such as
        gold, silver, copper, and platinum for macro context and hedging intuition.
        The goal is disciplined participation, not adrenaline trades.
      </p>

      <h2 class="reveal-on-scroll">Professional growth &amp; knowledge management</h2>

      <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
        Deep tech, enterprise AI governance, and organizational transformation are
        already central to my work; off the clock I treat learning like a craft. I use
        GTD for commitments and PARA to keep projects, areas, resources, and archives
        from collapsing into one overwhelming stream.
      </p>

      <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
        Personal knowledge management is almost a structured hobby: capturing ideas,
        linking them to client patterns and research, and turning that corpus into
        articles, talks, and clearer thinking the next time a board asks a hard
        question.
      </p>

      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li class="reveal-on-scroll">GTD for capture, clarify, and weekly review</li>
        <li class="reveal-on-scroll">PARA so reference material stays findable</li>
        <li class="reveal-on-scroll">Writing and speaking as the “output layer” for PKM</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <figure class="page-image page-figure reveal-on-scroll">
      <img
        src="/images/interests-outdoor-training.png"
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
        alt="Outdoor strength training on grass in bright daylight: kettlebells and gym equipment laid out for a session."
      />
    </figure>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
